WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.319
Let's prepare a restaurant booking brief with FormBridge. We'll follow a dinner enquiry at Juniper

2
00:00:05.319 --> 00:00:09.220
in Sydney, including a change of plans and a staff review.

3
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:15.784
A new visit starts with an empty brief. You can paste an existing conversation, with Customer and

4
00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:21.020
Staff labels, or add messages one at a time. For this enquiry, we'll add each message.

5
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:28.860
The customer asks for four people at Juniper in Sydney, on the tenth of October, at seven p.m. After

6
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.820
analysis, all five details appear in the brief, ready for review.

7
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:39.636
Now the customer says, actually, make that five guests, and sometime after eight. The brief updates

8
00:00:39.636 --> 00:00:46.180
the guest count. It keeps the time unresolved and asks for an exact time, rather than choosing one.

9
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:54.015
Switch to Staff and add the offer: eight thirty. The suggestion is visible in the conversation, but

10
00:00:54.015 --> 00:00:56.830
the brief still needs the customer's answer.

11
00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:04.311
Switch back to Customer. Yes, eight thirty is perfect. After that acceptance, the requested time

12
00:01:04.311 --> 00:01:08.200
becomes eight thirty and the brief is complete again.

13
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:15.471
Open the time detail to see its sources. Both the staff offer and the customer's acceptance are

14
00:01:15.471 --> 00:01:19.160
linked, so you can review the context behind the answer.

15
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:26.382
Open What changed to review earlier values. You can follow the change from four guests to five, and

16
00:01:26.382 --> 00:01:30.530
from seven p.m. to an open time preference, then to eight thirty.

17
00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:39.651
Use the pencil beside a detail to review or edit it. Here we save the five guests as a

18
00:01:39.651 --> 00:01:44.780
staff-reviewed value. Your edit is labelled and kept when new messages arrive.

19
00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:52.937
When the details are ready, approve the brief and download a copy for your team. You can choose a

20
00:01:52.937 --> 00:01:58.963
text brief or JSON. FormBridge prepares the handoff; it does not check availability or make the

21
00:01:58.963 --> 00:01:59.340
reservation.

22
00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:06.450
Choose New brief when you're ready for the next enquiry. Bring your own restaurant conversation and

23
00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.360
give every detail a place.
